  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1980s in Washington, a military officer is said to have helped sell President Ronald Reagan on SDI, the Strategic Defense Initiative, a plan for missile defence in space, by pointing to an alien threat the officer knew was false. Steven Greer, an activist who campaigns for UFO secrets to be made public, says a Colonel Hohman told him this, quoting him: \"We knew that was false, but it got billions of dollars for SDI.\" Greer also brings in President Jimmy Carter, and tells it to show how a fake alien danger could be used to win money and power."
